---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalDocument from '~/components/hia/LegalDocument.astro';
import { program, legal } from '~/data/program';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Program Terms',
  description: `The terms that apply when your child takes part in ${legal.entity}: enrolment, health and safety, and more.`,
};

const email = program.contactEmail
  ? `<a href="mailto:${program.contactEmail}">${program.contactEmail}</a>`
  : 'the enquiry form on our website';
const contactLines = [
  program.contactEmail && `Email: ${email}`,
  program.contactPhone && `Phone: ${program.contactPhone}`,
]
  .filter(Boolean)
  .join('<br />');
const contactBlock = `<p>${legal.entity}<br />${program.city}${contactLines ? '<br />' + contactLines : ''}</p>${
  program.contactEmail ? '' : '<p>Please reach us through ' + email + '.</p>'
}`;

// DRAFT for legal review. Business rules mirror the FAQ and src/data/program.ts; edit both together.
const sections = [
  {
    title: 'About these terms',
    body: `
      <p>These terms govern your child’s participation in ${legal.entity} (the “program”), run in ${program.city} by ${legal.operator} (“we”, “us”). By enrolling a child, you agree to them. Please read them together with our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      <p>You confirm that you are the child’s parent or legal guardian, that you are at least 18 years old, and that you have authority to enrol the child and to agree to these terms on their behalf.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'The program',
    body: `
      <p>The program is a character enrichment program for children in ${program.grades}. It runs for ${program.sessions} weekly sessions of ${program.sessionLength} each, with up to ${program.maxGroupSize} children per group. Sessions use stories, conversation and hands-on activities to explore gratitude, kindness, empathy, friendship, respect, courage and helping others.</p>
      <p>Dates, times and locations are announced separately and confirmed to enrolled families. We may adjust the schedule or venue where reasonably necessary and will give you as much notice as we can.</p>
      <p>The program is educational enrichment. It is not counselling, therapy, childcare or medical advice, and it does not replace support from a qualified professional if your child needs it. We cannot promise any particular outcome for an individual child.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Enrolment, fees and cancellations',
    body: `
      <p>${program.upcomingNote} Enrolment is not yet open. Any fees, payment methods and cancellation and refund terms will be confirmed before a program opens for enrolment, and these terms will be updated at that time.</p>
      <p>Until then, enquiring about a program does not reserve a place or create any obligation for you or for us. You agree to give accurate information and to tell us promptly if it changes. Group sizes are limited, so places will be offered in the order enrolments are completed.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Missed sessions',
    body: `
      <p>If your child is unwell or otherwise misses a session, please let us know. We will send home that week’s take-home reminder card so your child can stay connected to the group. We cannot guarantee make-up sessions.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Health, safety and supervision',
    body: `
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Health information.</strong> You must tell us about any allergies, medical conditions, medication or other needs when you enrol your child, and keep that information up to date. We keep it, with your emergency contact, with us at every session.</li>
        <li><strong>Illness.</strong> Please keep your child at home if they are unwell, including with a fever, vomiting or any contagious illness.</li>
        <li><strong>Drop-off and pick-up.</strong> ${program.dropOff} Please do not send anyone to collect your child whom we have not been told about in advance.</li>
        <li><strong>Emergencies.</strong> If your child is injured or becomes seriously ill, we will contact you and your emergency contact straight away. You authorize us to call 911 or seek urgent medical care for your child if we cannot reach you in time. You remain responsible for any resulting medical or ambulance costs.</li>
        <li><strong>Small groups.</strong> We keep groups to ${program.maxGroupSize} children or fewer so that every child can be seen, heard and supported.</li>
      </ul>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Behaviour and participation',
    body: `
      <p>We aim for a calm, respectful space where every child belongs. We will work with you and your child first if a child finds it hard to take part safely or respectfully. If behaviour continues to put the safety or wellbeing of the child or others at risk, we may ask you to collect your child early or, as a last resort, to withdraw from the program. Where we do, we will discuss a fair outcome with you.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Photos and media',
    body: `
      <p>We will not take, use or share photos, video or recordings that identify a child without the permission of that child’s parent or guardian. Where you give permission, you may withdraw it at any time by contacting us via ${email}, and we will stop using the material going forward.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Risk and liability',
    body: `
      <p>Children’s activities carry some ordinary risk, such as minor bumps and scrapes from craft work and moving around a room. We take reasonable care to supervise children and keep the space and materials safe, and you agree to follow our health and safety instructions.</p>
      <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for loss or damage that is not caused by our negligence or breach of these terms, or for indirect or consequential losses. Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited, or any rights you have under Ontario consumer protection law.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Program materials and this website',
    body: `
      <p>The program content, curriculum, illustrations, text and design on this website and in session materials belong to ${legal.operator} or are used with permission. You may use take-home materials with your family, but you may not copy, sell or distribute the program materials without our written permission.</p>
      <p>We work to keep this website accurate, but we may change or correct it at any time, and dates, availability and details here do not form a binding offer until confirmed in your enrolment.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Privacy',
    body: `
      <p>How we collect, use and protect your family’s information is explained in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which forms part of these terms.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Governing law and disputes',
    body: `
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that apply there. If a disagreement arises, please contact us first so we can try to resolve it directly and fairly. Any dispute we cannot resolve will be decided by the courts of Ontario.</p>
      <p>If any part of these terms is found to be unenforceable, the rest remain in effect.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Changes to these terms',
    body: `
      <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The terms in force when you enrol apply to your child’s participation in that program. The effective date at the top shows the current version.</p>`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Contact us',
    body: `
      ${contactBlock}`,
  },
];
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <LegalDocument
    title="Program Terms"
    intro={`Plain, fair terms for families: how enrolment works, and how we look after your child.`}
    sections={sections}
    related={{ text: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy' }}
  />
</Layout>
